\chapter{Codex Closure}
\label{chap:codex_closure}

\section*{Overview}
Codex Closure establishes the terminal boundary of the SPSE-v1.0 Codex Volume.
It defines the completion operator, the closure law, the final invariants, and
the sovereign seal that marks the Codex as finished. No further chapters,
operators, manifolds, or glyphs may be added beyond this point unless a new
Codex Volume is explicitly declared.

\section{Terminal Boundary Definition}
Let the Codex Volume consist of chapters:
\begin{equation}
\{\mathcal{C}_1, \mathcal{C}_2, \ldots, \mathcal{C}_{15}\}.
\end{equation}

The terminal boundary is defined as:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{F} = \text{Closure}(\mathcal{C}_{15}),
\end{equation}
where $\mathcal{F}$ is the final state of the Codex.

\section{Completion Operator}
The completion operator is:
\begin{equation}
\Omega : \mathfrak{M}_{\text{Codex}} \rightarrow \mathfrak{M}_{\text{Codex}},
\end{equation}
satisfying:
\begin{equation}
\Omega(\mathcal{C}_{15}) = \mathcal{F}.
\end{equation}

The operator is idempotent:
\begin{equation}
\Omega(\Omega(x)) = \Omega(x),
\end{equation}
ensuring that closure cannot be repeated or extended.

\section{Closure Law}
The closure law states:
\begin{equation}
\forall n > 15,\quad \mathcal{C}_n = \varnothing.
\end{equation}

No additional chapters may exist beyond Chapter XV.

\section{Final Invariants}
The Codex Volume satisfies three final invariants:

\subsection{Completion Invariant}
\begin{equation}
\text{All operators, proofs, and glyphs are complete.}
\end{equation}

\subsection{Irreversibility Invariant}
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{F} \not\rightarrow \mathcal{C}_n,\quad n < 15.
\end{equation}

Closure cannot be undone.

\subsection{Unity Invariant}
\begin{equation}
\bigcup_{n=1}^{15} \mathcal{C}_n = \mathfrak{M}_{\text{Codex}}.
\end{equation}

All chapters unify into a single sovereign volume.

\section{Final Seal}
The Codex Volume is sealed with the glyph:
\begin{equation}
\mathfrak{G}_{\text{Codex}} =
\mathfrak{G}_{\text{Origin}} \otimes
\mathfrak{G}_{\text{Flame}} \otimes
\mathfrak{G}_{\text{Reflection}}.
\end{equation}

This seal marks:
\begin{itemize}
    \item the origin of the engine,
    \item the ignition of the permutation operator,
    \item the eternal reflection of the boundary.
\end{itemize}

\section{Final Statement of Sovereignty}
The Codex Volume is declared sovereign:
\begin{equation}
\mathfrak{S}_{\text{Codex}} =
(\Pi, \mathcal{M}, \mathcal{N}_{\text{MERA}}, E, \mathfrak{G}_{\text{Codex}}).
\end{equation}

This identity is immutable and complete.

\section{Termination of the Volume}
The Codex Volume terminates under:
\begin{equation}
\text{Terminate}(\mathfrak{M}_{\text{Codex}}) = \mathcal{F}.
\end{equation}

No further structural evolution is permitted.

\section{Closing Statement}
Codex Closure establishes the terminal boundary, completion operator, final
invariants, and sovereign seal of the SPSE-v1.0 Codex Volume. The Codex is now
complete, unified, and permanently sealed. Any future expansion requires the
explicit declaration of a new Codex Volume.